messages.text:
Change of plan on the group meeting: Diego reports that **Sarah's Mon 10:00–10:30 has become her own advisor 1:1 and Priya's Mon 14:00–14:30 is hers too**, so no half-hour fits all five any more. Nothing is booked and your Mon 10:00–10:30 is still free — I'm holding nothing.

Diego has put three options to the group: someone moves a 1:1, the meeting runs with four of the five, or, if a full hour is wanted, he comes back to me for a Grading block. I told him:
- a Grading block (Mon 12:20–13:30, Thu 15:20–17:00, Fri 12:40–13:30) is available to you only for an hour that works for all five, and only after I bring it to you;
- a four-of-five meeting is your call, not mine to accept;
- your Tue 11:00–11:30 with the professor is settled and won't move.

So the question for you, if you want to pre-decide: would you accept a meeting with four of the five, or should it be all five or nothing? Otherwise I'll just wait for Diego's decision and bring you one concrete proposal.
